# Build Risk Guard

Pre-flight checks before builds/tests and before declaring work done.

## Shell: PowerShell has no `&&`

```powershell
cargo fmt --check; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
cargo clippy -- -D warnings; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }
```

## Locked desktop binary (`os error 5`)

Running `ade-desktop-app.exe` or `ade.exe serve` locks targets. Stop those processes, or scope builds (`--exclude ade-desktop-app`). Lock errors are environment issues — do not "fix" code for them.

## Money: never reintroduce `f64`

All monetary values use `ade_core::Money` (i64 micro-dollars). Convert `f64`/USD only at UI/CLI boundaries.

## const fn

Avoid non-const trait methods (`Ord::max`/`min`) in `const fn`; use explicit branches.

## Definition of done

Pass: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test`, and `tsc --noEmit` in `apps/desktop`. Never disable lint/security tools to make a build pass.

## Safety invariants

Never commit two write-capable agents on one checkout. Never read/quote secrets. Never merge/deploy without human approval.
